Lua Lesson 2 — here it is fresh so you don't have to scroll:
One concept: functions. In JS it's function add(a, b) { return a + b }. In Lua there are no curly braces — the function ends with the word end, and no types:
Lua
local cash = 500

local function addMoney(current, amount)
    return current + amount
end

cash = addMoney(cash, 220)
print("Cash after paycheck: $" .. cash)
